voice-lab.patch modifies this pinned source at preparation time. It is not a
replacement inference model. The patch owns these integration corrections:
- private IPv4 loopback listener with bearer authentication;
- supplied system instructions in native turn and duplex prompt formats;
- final queued text delivery and acknowledgments for silent duplex steps;
- explicit speech drain and truthful text/acoustic completion boundaries;
- final duplex acoustic decoding beyond the one-second intermediate chunk limit.

The runtime records the patch SHA-256 in experiment reports. Preparation rejects
unexpected source changes and records successful builds only after CMake exits.
The downloaded model weights have their own Apache-2.0 license and provenance;
this MIT notice applies to the native source, not the model checkpoints.
